---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Drip from '../components/Drip.astro';
import { SOCIAL_IMAGES } from '../config/site';
---

<Base
  title="About Michael Jolley"
  description="Michael Jolley is a longtime software developer and teacher sharing honest lessons about .NET, Windows, and developer tools."
  active="about"
  image={SOCIAL_IMAGES.about}
>
  <main id="main" class="subpage about-page">
    <section class="about-stage about-hero">
      <div class="page-ghost" aria-hidden="true">HELLO.</div>
      <div class="about-stage-inner">
        <div>
          <span class="signal-label">Michael Jolley / Bald Bearded Builder</span>
          <h1>I teach the way I learned: out loud.</h1>
          <p>Real code, honest tradeoffs, and the mistakes that make the lesson stick.</p>
        </div>
        <img src="/images/type-stage/laugh.webp" alt="Michael Jolley laughing" width="1600" height="1139" fetchpriority="high" />
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-story">
      <div class="story-kicker">
        <span>Since 1999</span>
        <strong>20+ years writing C#</strong>
      </div>
      <div class="story-copy">
        <h2>I am Michael. Most folks know me as the Bald Bearded Builder.</h2>
        <p>I have spent more than two decades building software, leading developer communities, and teaching people how the pieces fit together. These days I spend most of my time with .NET, Windows, and the tools that help us get useful work done.</p>
        <p>I do not pretend every demo works on the first try. If something breaks, we look at why. If a pattern has a cost, we talk about it. The polished answer is useful, but the road to that answer is usually where the lesson lives.</p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>Good teaching does not hide the mess. It gives you enough context to clean up your own.</p>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="about-principles">
      <header class="section-header light">
        <span>What you will find here</span>
        <h2>The meat and potatoes.</h2>
      </header>
      <div class="principle-grid">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Build the real thing.</h3><p>Examples should survive contact with an actual project, not just a perfect ten line sample.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Explain the tradeoff.</h3><p>A tool is only useful when you know when to reach for it and when to leave it in the drawer.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Learn together.</h3><p>I know a lot. I do not know everything. That makes the conversation better.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Drip uid="about" />
  </main>
</Base>
